      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "For the past two years, Tacoma Family Medicine, Tacoma, Washington. has integrated a curriculum in psychosocial aspects of coronary care with the Coronary Care Unit rotation taken by third-year residents. Goals of the curriculum are to provide information, to foster the development of psychosocial strategies for patient and family care, and to develop greater insight and awareness on the part of residents regarding the psychosocial aspects of coronary care. Attempts are made to meet these goals in a context as closely tied to the clinical management of patients and families as possible. Topics addressed include the biopsychosocial medical model, patient and family responses to cardiac illness, sexual concerns of the coronary patient and spouse, and issues related to cardiac rehabilitation. The format for the curriculum involves didactic presentations, group discussions, and case consultations."},
